cument\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Continuity-of-Care/Advice-to-the-Profession-Continuity-of-Care\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Advice to the Profession: Protecting Personal Health Information\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy Document\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Protecting-Personal-Health-Information/Advice-to-the-Profession-Protecting-Personal-Healt\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Availability and Coverage\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy Document\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Availability-and-Coverage\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Protecting Personal Health Information\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy Document\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Protecting-Personal-Health-Information\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"_tool_name\\\": \\\"opa_policy_check\\\",\\n  \\\"_citation_count\\\": 12\\n}\",\"annotations\":null,\"meta\":null}", "type": "function_call_output"}','2025-09-27 23:49:22');
INSERT INTO agent_messages VALUES(12,'test_session','{"id": "msg_68d87803e77c81948c39dc5b9076a5f009b5f7d4b6261803", "content": [{"annotations": [], "text": "### CPSO Policy on Telemedicine\n\n**Direct Answer:**\nThe College of Physicians and Surgeons of Ontario (CPSO) has established several guidelines and policies regarding telemedicine, particularly under the umbrella of \u201cVirtual Care.\u201d There are mandatory expectations that physicians must adhere to when engaging in virtual care practices.\n\n**Current Guidance:**\n1. **Virtual Care Policy**: This policy outlines the essential considerations for physicians providing care through virtual means.\n   - [CPSO - Virtual Care](https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Virtual-Care)\n\n2. **Advice to the Profession: Virtual Care**: This document provides further recommendations alongside the mandatory expectations for best practices in virtual care.\n   - [CPSO - Advice to the Profession: Virtual Care](https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Virtual-Care/Advice-to-the-Profession-Virtual-Care)\n\n3. **Continuity of Care**: This advice emphasizes the importance of maintaining continuity of care, which is critical in virtual consultations.\n   - [CPSO - Advice to the Profession: Continuity of Care](https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Continuity-of-Care/Advice-to-the-Profession-Continuity-of-Care)\n\n4. **Protecting Personal Health Information**: In telemedicine, safeguarding patient information is paramount. This document outlines necessary precautions to protect patient data.\n   - [CPSO - Advice to the Profession: Protecting Personal Health Information](https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Protecting-Personal-Health-Information/Advice-to-the-Profession-Protecting-Personal-Healt)\n\n5. **Availability and Coverage**: Covers expectations related to physician availability and patient coverage during remote consultations.\n   - [CPSO - Availability and Coverage](https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Availability-and-Coverage)\n\n**Implementation Notes:**\n- Physicians must ensure that they comply with these policies to provide safe and effective virtual care.\n- It''s crucial to maintain clear communication with patients and uphold their confidentiality during virtual visits.\n- Physicians should be prepared to assess if a virtual consultation is appropriate for each patient''s specific needs.\n\n**Related Resources:**\n- For more information, refer to the CPSO''s guidance on advertising and other related policies that may impact virtual care practices.\n  - [CPSO - Advice to the Profession: Advertising](https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Advertising/Advice-to-the-Profession-Advertising)\n\n**Currency Note:**\nThe information retrieved is current as of now, reflecting ongoing CPSO policies concerning virtual care. Please verify the above links for the latest updates directly from CPSO.", "type": "output_text", "logprobs": []}], "role": "assistant", "status": "completed", "type": "message"}','2025-09-27 23:49:31');
