ontrolled\\\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \\\"policy_level\\\": \\\"expectation\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"point\\\": \\\"Advice to the Profession: Protecting Personal Health Information: Mandatory expectation\\\",\\n      \\\"citations\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"source\\\": \\\"Advice to the Profession: Protecting Personal Health Information\\\",\\n          \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n          \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy\\\",\\n          \\\"page\\\": null,\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Protecting-Personal-Health-Information/Advice-to-the-Profession-Protecting-Personal-Healt\\\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \\\"policy_level\\\": \\\"expectation\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"advice\\\": [],\\n  \\\"related\\\": [],\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": 0.9099999999999999,\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"CPSO Guidance for ''virtual care documentation'': Found 15 mandatory expectation(s)\\\",\\n  \\\"citations\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Virtual Care\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy\\\",\\n      \\\"page\\\": null,\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Virtual-Care\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Advice to the Profession: Virtual Care\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy\\\",\\n      \\\"page\\\": null,\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Virtual-Care/Advice-to-the-Profession-Virtual-Care\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Advice to the Profession: Medical Records Documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy\\\",\\n      \\\"page\\\": null,\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Medical-Records-Documentation/Advice-to-the-Profession-Medical-Records-Documenta\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Advice to the Profession: Delegation of Controlled Acts\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy\\\",\\n      \\\"page\\\": null,\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Delegation-of-Controlled-Acts/Advice-to-the-Profession-Delegation-of-Controlled\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Advice to the Profession: Protecting Personal Health Information\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy\\\",\\n      \\\"page\\\": null,\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Protecting-Personal-Health-Information/Advice-to-the-Profession-Protecting-Personal-Healt\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Virtual Care\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy Document\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Virtual-Care\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Advice to the Profession: Virtual Care\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy Document\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Virtual-Care/Advice-to-the-Profession-Virtual-Care\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Advice to the Profession: Medical Records Documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy Document\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Medical-Records-Documentation/Advice-to-the-Profession-Medical-Records-Documenta\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Advice to the Profession: Delegation of Controlled Acts\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy Document\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Delegation-of-Controlled-Acts/Advice-to-the-Profession-Delegation-of-Controlled\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Advice to the Profession: Protecting Personal Health Information\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy Document\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Protecting-Personal-Health-Information/Advice-to-the-Profession-Protecting-Personal-Healt\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"_tool_name\\\": \\\"opa_policy_check\\\",\\n  \\\"_citation_count\\\": 10\\n}\",\"annotations\":null,\"meta\":null}", "type": "function_call_output"}','2025-09-29 01:25:31');
INSERT INTO agent_messages VALUES(42,'26cb378e-4e35-4a04-9330-df54886868ec','{"id": "msg_68d9e00cd6a48196bff87983f6f3cea401148f0c530f0049", "content": [{"annotations": [], "text": "**SUMMARY**: The CPSO mandates specific documentation requirements for virtual care, emphasizing that all virtual interactions and decisions must be appropriately recorded. This aligns with general medical documentation guidelines but necessitates particular attention to the unique aspects of virtual care.\n\n**DETAILED RESPONSE**:\nThe CPSO has established comprehensive policies on documenting virtual care that practitioners must adhere to. Key requirements include:\n\n1. **Comprehensive Documentation**: All virtual care encounters must be documented thoroughly, including the nature of the interaction, clinical decisions made, and follow-up plans. This ensures continuity of care and accountability.\n\n2. **Medical Record Requirements**: Practitioners should follow the guidelines laid out in the [CPSO - Advice to the Profession: Medical Records Documentation](https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Medical-Records-Documentation/Advice-to-the-Profession-Medical-Records-Documenta) to maintain consistent medical records.\n\n3. **Confidentiality and Privacy**: Documentation must protect patient privacy in accordance with the [CPSO - Protecting Personal Health Information](https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Protecting-Personal-Health-Information/Advice-to-the-Profession-Protecting-Personal-Healt) guidelines.\n\n4. **Compliance with Specific Policies**: Practitioners are required to adhere to the expectations set forth in the [CPSO - Virtual Care Policy](https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Virtual-Care) and related advice documents, which emphasize the need for clarity in documentation practices specific to virtual health settings.\n\n5. **Periodic Review**: As technology and procedures can change, ensure that documentation practices are regularly reviewed and updated in accordance with the latest CPSO policies.\n\nThese expectations aim to enhance the quality of care provided through virtual means while also safeguarding patient information. For a detailed understanding of these requirements, refer to the CPSO\u2019s official documents linked above.\n\n**Currency Note**: This information is based on the most current CPSO guidance as of now.", "type": "output_text", "logprobs": []}], "role": "assistant", "status": "completed", "type": "message"}','2025-09-29 01:25:38');
