egation of Controlled Acts: Mandatory expectation\\\",\\n      \\\"citations\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"source\\\": \\\"Advice to the Profession: Delegation of Controlled Acts\\\",\\n          \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n          \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy\\\",\\n          \\\"page\\\": null,\\n          \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Delegation-of-Controlled-Acts/Advice-to-the-Profession-Delegation-of-Controlled\\\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \\\"policy_level\\\": \\\"expectation\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"advice\\\": [],\\n  \\\"related\\\": [],\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": 0.9099999999999999,\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"CPSO Guidance for ''virtual care documentation'': Found 15 mandatory expectation(s)\\\",\\n  \\\"citations\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Virtual Care\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy\\\",\\n      \\\"page\\\": null,\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Virtual-Care\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Advice to the Profession: Virtual Care\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy\\\",\\n      \\\"page\\\": null,\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Virtual-Care/Advice-to-the-Profession-Virtual-Care\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Advice to the Profession: Medical Records Documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy\\\",\\n      \\\"page\\\": null,\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Medical-Records-Documentation/Advice-to-the-Profession-Medical-Records-Documenta\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Medical Records Documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy\\\",\\n      \\\"page\\\": null,\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Medical-Records-Documentation\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Advice to the Profession: Delegation of Controlled Acts\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy\\\",\\n      \\\"page\\\": null,\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Delegation-of-Controlled-Acts/Advice-to-the-Profession-Delegation-of-Controlled\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Virtual Care\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy Document\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Virtual-Care\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Advice to the Profession: Virtual Care\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy Document\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Virtual-Care/Advice-to-the-Profession-Virtual-Care\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Advice to the Profession: Medical Records Documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy Document\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Medical-Records-Documentation/Advice-to-the-Profession-Medical-Records-Documenta\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Medical Records Documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy Document\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Medical-Records-Documentation\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"Advice to the Profession: Delegation of Controlled Acts\\\",\\n      \\\"source_org\\\": \\\"cpso\\\",\\n      \\\"loc\\\": \\\"Policy Document\\\",\\n      \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Delegation-of-Controlled-Acts/Advice-to-the-Profession-Delegation-of-Controlled\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"_tool_name\\\": \\\"opa_policy_check\\\",\\n  \\\"_citation_count\\\": 10\\n}\",\"annotations\":null,\"meta\":null}", "type": "function_call_output"}','2025-09-29 02:36:57');
INSERT INTO agent_messages VALUES(70,'7e901880-352e-4231-ac7c-ede3c8d9f8a5','{"id": "msg_68d9f0cafb508190a3aca9c264703bfc09f7ad4c91d8d51a", "content": [{"annotations": [], "text": "### EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n\nThe CPSO sets clear requirements for virtual care documentation to ensure quality, continuity, and accountability in patient care. Documentation must be accurate, timely, and include all relevant clinical and administrative details of the virtual encounter. Physicians are required to follow the same standards for documentation as they would for in-person visits, ensuring that virtual care records are complete and accessible as part of the patient''s overall medical record.\n\n### DETAILED CLINICAL GUIDANCE\n\n#### Policy Framework & Requirements\n- **Virtual Care Policy**: Physicians must document virtual care interactions comprehensively, including patient consent, technology used, and the limitations of virtual platforms ([CPSO - Virtual Care](https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Virtual-Care)).\n  \n- **Medical Records Documentation**: Aligns with the documentation standards applicable to in-person care. Records must capture the clinical interaction accurately and be maintained in a manner that supports continuity of care ([CPSO - Medical Records Documentation](https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Medical-Records-Documentation)).\n\n#### Clinical Pathways & Standards\n- Documentation should clearly detail the patient''s condition, the treatment plan discussed, any prescriptions given, and the follow-up plan. This ensures that any subsequent healthcare provider can understand the care provided.\n\n#### Program Specifics\n- Physicians must ensure that virtual care records are integrated with existing medical records and systems, facilitating access and promoting interoperability.\n\n#### Implementation Guidance\n- Use secure electronic systems that are compliant with privacy regulations to document and store virtual care encounters.\n- Documentation should occur in real-time or as soon as possible after the consultation to maintain accuracy.\n\n#### Recent Updates & Changes\n- Regular updates and clarifications have been provided in CPSO advice documents to reflect technological and practice changes ([CPSO - Advice to the Profession: Virtual Care](https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Virtual-Care/Advice-to-the-Profession-Virtual-Care)).\n\n#### Related Considerations\n- Ensure all team members involved in patient care have access to the documented records, in line with data-sharing policies.\n\n#### Additional Resources\n- [CPSO - Virtual Care Policy](https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Virtual-Care)\n- [CPSO - Medical Records Documentation](https://www.cpso.on.ca/en/Physicians/Policies-Guidance/Policies/Medical-Records-Documentation)\n\n### Currency Note\nThe guidance was verified as of the latest CPSO policies, upholding the requirements for secure, detailed, and accessible documentation of virtual care encounters.\n\n### Sources & Tool Contributions\n- **MCP Tools Used**:\n  - **opa_policy_check**: CPSO policies on virtual care and medical records were retrieved, providing comprehensive mandatory expectations.\n  \n  No additional web search was required as the primary MCP tool provided adequate detailed information.", "type": "output_text", "logprobs": []}], "role": "assistant", "status": "completed", "type": "message"}','2025-09-29 02:37:17');
